From: Ethan Blanch <ethan.blanch@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:45:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] compat: define SYS_SECCOMP only for Android libc

glibc declares SYS_SECCOMP as an enum constant in <bits/siginfo-consts.h>
(pulled in by <signal.h> under _GNU_SOURCE). Defining it as a macro first
turns the enum into "enum { 1 = 1, ... }" and the build fails with
"expected identifier" in syscall/enter.c. Bionic has no such definition,
which is why Termux builds are unaffected.

Only needed for static glibc builds; no behaviour change on Android libc.
---
diff --git a/src/compat.h b/src/compat.h
index 53300b8..25eae43 100644
--- a/src/compat.h
+++ b/src/compat.h
@@ -261,7 +261,11 @@
 #    ifndef NT_ARM_SYSTEM_CALL
 #        define NT_ARM_SYSTEM_CALL		0x404
 #    endif
-#    ifndef SYS_SECCOMP
+#    /* Modified 2026-09-26 for uls-proot (github.com/ItsPhysip/uls-proot):
+     * only define this for Android libc.  glibc declares SYS_SECCOMP as an
+     * enum in <bits/siginfo-consts.h>, which this macro breaks when
+     * building proot statically against glibc. */
+#    if !defined(SYS_SECCOMP) && defined(__ANDROID__)
 #        define SYS_SECCOMP 1
 #    endif
 
